    answer: "A few seconds each morning for SPF on the face, ears, and neck; sunglasses and a hat by the door; choosing the shady side of the street; keeping sleeves on in the car; skipping the tanning bed; and a quick skin glance in the mirror each month. None is dramatic, but repeated over decades they meaningfully lower skin cancer and aging. Our prevention overview ties them together.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  faqPageJsonLd(`${canonical}#melanoma-diagnosed`, melanomaDiagnosedFaq),
  faqPageJsonLd(`${canonical}#bcc-diagnosed`, bccDiagnosedFaq),
  faqPageJsonLd(`${canonical}#melanoma-living`, melanomaLivingFaq),
