                    <Icon name="lucide:chevron-right" size={18} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-teal transition-transform group-open:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true" />
                    <span>Where in the skin does melanoma start, and why can it sometimes spread?</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Melanoma begins in melanocytes along the border between the epidermis, the outer layer of skin, and the dermis beneath it. Early on it spreads sideways and is easy to cure. If it isn't removed, it can grow downward into the dermis, where blood and lymph vessels give cells a route to lymph nodes and distant organs. That's why <a href="/melanoma/breslow-depth-explained" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">depth matters</a> so much.</p>
