                    <p>It means metastasis — cancer cells breaking away and traveling through blood or lymph to lymph nodes or organs — happens in far fewer than 1 in 1,000 basal cell carcinomas. Almost all stay put as a local growth on the skin. That's why staging scans and lymph node checks aren't routine for BCC, unlike <a href="/melanoma" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">melanoma</a>. The main risk is local damage if it's left alone.</p>
