                    <span>After being told I have basal cell carcinoma, what are the typical next steps?</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Usually your dermatologist reviews the biopsy result with you, explains the subtype and location, and recommends a treatment — most often a minor in-office procedure scheduled within a few weeks. There's rarely a need for scans or blood tests. You'll get wound-care instructions afterward and a follow-up skin exam. Because a first BCC raises the odds of another, regular full-skin checks become part of your routine — our <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/recurrence-prevention" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">recurrence-prevention guide</a> has details.</p>
