                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>They weigh the subtype, size, and location, whether it's a first tumor or a recurrence, and your overall health and preferences. Aggressive subtypes or spots on the face usually get surgery, often Mohs, for the highest cure rate. Small, superficial tumors on the trunk may suit scraping and burning, cryotherapy, or a prescription cream. Cure rates and trade-offs differ. Our <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">BCC treatment options</a> compares them.</p>
