                    <p>These labels predict how likely a tumor is to come back after treatment, not whether it will spread. High-risk features include an aggressive <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/types" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">subtype</a> under the microscope, larger size, location on the "mask" area of the face, ears, hands, or feet, poorly defined borders, a recurrent tumor, or a weakened immune system. High-risk BCCs usually get Mohs surgery for the best chance of a lasting cure.</p>
