                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Mohs surgery removes the tumor layer by layer, checking 100% of each layer's edges under a microscope during the same visit before closing the wound. That gives the highest cure rate while sparing the most healthy tissue — valuable on the face, where a standard excision samples only part of the margin and removes a wider safety border. It's favored for high-risk, recurrent, or cosmetically sensitive BCCs. See <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">BCC treatment options</a>.</p>
