                    <span>What are the pros and cons of topical treatments like imiquimod or 5-FU?</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Creams such as imiquimod or 5-fluorouracil are applied at home for several weeks and leave no surgical scar, which appeals for small, superficial BCCs on the trunk or limbs. The trade-offs: cure rates are lower than surgery, the skin gets red, crusted, and sore during treatment, and margins can't be checked, so follow-up matters. They aren't used for nodular or facial tumors. Our <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treatment options</a> page compares approaches.</p>
