                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>For carefully chosen low-risk BCCs — small, superficial, away from the face — electrodesiccation and curettage (scraping then burning the base) cures roughly 90 to 95 percent, and cryotherapy (freezing with liquid nitrogen) is similar in expert hands. Both are quick and inexpensive but leave a pale, round scar and don't allow margin checking. They're avoided for aggressive subtypes or high-risk sites, where surgery is safer.</p>
