                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>A small removal closed with a few stitches typically means mild soreness, a bandage for a day or two, stitches out in one to two weeks, and a thin line that fades over months. Larger removals — or repairs using a skin flap or graft — bring more swelling, bruising, activity limits, and a longer-healing scar. Your team gives site-specific wound care. Our <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/recovery-after-surgery" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">recovery-after-surgery</a> page has a timeline.</p>
