                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Raise it before the procedure, not after. Ask where the scar will sit, how long it will be, which repair options exist, and whether <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">Mohs</a> would spare more tissue. Ask about scar-care steps — taping, silicone gel, sun protection, and when laser or revision could help if you're unhappy later. A good surgeon expects these questions and will plan the closure with your appearance in mind.</p>
