                    <p>Yes — it's routine and expected, and BCC's slow growth means a short delay to get one is rarely a problem. A second dermatologist or a Mohs surgeon can confirm the biopsy reading and review whether surgery, radiation, or a topical option best fits your tumor, your other health conditions, and your priorities. Bring your <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/biopsy-meaning" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">pathology report</a> and photos so the discussion is concrete.</p>
