                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Yes, ongoing. After a BCC, about 4 in 10 people develop another skin cancer within five years, so dermatologists usually schedule full-skin exams every 6 to 12 months, sometimes more often at first. Visits include checking the treated site for recurrence and scanning the rest of your skin for new spots. Monthly self-checks fill the gaps between visits. Our <a href="/basal-cell-carcinoma/recurrence-prevention" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">recurrence-prevention</a> page explains the schedule.</p>
