                    <p>Mohs is favored when tissue preservation and the highest cure rate matter most: tumors on the face, ears, lips, nose, hands, feet, or genitals; large or poorly defined lesions; aggressive growth patterns; perineural invasion; recurrent SCC; and tumors in people with weakened immunity. The surgeon removes tissue in thin layers, checking each one under the microscope until margins are clear. See which spots count as <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/high-risk-locations" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">high-risk locations</a>.</p>
