                    <p>Options depend on risk. Surgical excision cuts out the tumor with a margin of normal skin and stitches the wound. Mohs surgery maps margins layer by layer for high-risk or cosmetically sensitive sites. Curettage and electrodesiccation scrapes and burns small, superficial low-risk lesions. Radiation treats tumors that can't be operated on or adds control afterward. Advanced disease may use immunotherapy. See our <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treatment options page</a> for details.</p>
