                    <p>Perineural invasion means cancer cells are tracking along or around a nerve, seen on the pathology slide. It signals a higher chance of local recurrence and spread because tumor can travel unseen along the nerve. Treatment often becomes more aggressive: Mohs or wider excision, imaging such as MRI to trace the nerve, and radiation after surgery when larger nerves are involved. It's one of the standard <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/staging-and-grading" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">high-risk features</a>.</p>
