                    <p>Some AKs do fade on their own, especially if sun exposure drops, and studies show a fair number clear over a year. But many of those return, and a small share progress toward squamous cell carcinoma. Because no one can predict which lesions will regress and which will advance, dermatologists usually treat AKs or keep them under close watch rather than ignoring them. Our <a href="/actinic-keratosis/treat-now-vs-watch" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treat now vs. watch guide</a> weighs the options.</p>
