                    <p>It means the abnormal cells in an AK sit on a spectrum. In an AK, the changes stay in the top layer of skin. If more mutations accumulate, those cells can break through into deeper tissue and become an invasive <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">squamous cell carcinoma</a> (SCC), a common skin cancer. Some experts even consider AK the earliest form of SCC. Treating an AK removes those cells before that step can happen.</p>
