                    <p>The biggest factor is lifetime ultraviolet exposure, so people who worked or played outdoors for years, or used tanning beds, accumulate more. Fair skin that burns easily, light eyes, blond or red hair, older age, living closer to the equator, and a history of blistering sunburns all raise the odds. A weakened immune system — from an organ transplant or certain medications — sharply increases both AK numbers and their risk of progressing.</p>
